OL,3,GNEWSAFinal weeks for Gabriel's Wharf
OL,4,Aafter almost 40 years
OL,5,
OL,6,FA group of independent businesses will
OL,7,Fbe evicted from their site on London's
OL,8,FSouth Bank this month to make way for
OL,9,Fredevelopment.
OL,11,FGabriel's Wharf, which has existed
OL,12,Fsince 1988, is home to around 20
OL,13,Findependent businesses, including art
OL,14,Fgalleries and food artisans.
OL,16,F"Everybody loves it and we just feel so
OL,17,Fsad," said Frances Bingham, one of the
OL,18,Fco-owners of Potters' Yard Arts. "It's
OL,19,Fone of the few places left in London
OL,20,Fthat has that lovely, happy, innocent
OL,21,Fkind of feeling about it."
OL,23,APub: 12-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
